WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.220
<b>Devil</b>

3
00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:01.620
I'm falling! I'm falling!
I'm falling! I'm falling!

4
00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.030
[LUFFY]
Whew!

5
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.330
Good! Safe and sound!

6
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.040
Man that wore me out. I'm...

7
00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.900
"Safe and sound" my butt!
I thought I was gonna die!

8
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.370
What was I supposed to do?

9
00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.470
You were the one that said

10
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.610
we couldn't use the elevator
'cause we'd get caught!

11
00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.680
I didn't have a choice!

12
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.210
That doesn't mean
"Hey, let's jump down," idiot!

13
00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:31.180
You can't glide around like

14
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.000
that square-nosed
shipwright, got it?!

15
00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.820
Right, sorry about that.

16
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.360
[NAMI]
Whatever. It's fine
since we're safe now.

17
00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.260
Then stop hitting me!

18
00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.470
However, we might not be safe for long.

19
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.670
[LUFFY]
We won't?
Why not? What's wrong?

20
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.940
[NAMI]
This island's
topography and climate.

21
00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.010
With this much wind blowing,

22
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.650
and the atmospheric
pressure falling so rapidly,

23
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.720
there's likely going to be a typhoon here
tonight.

24
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.320
This place is called
"The City of Water."

25
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.390
Think about it:

26
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.860
Its greatest weakness
would have to be flooding.

27
00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.020
Okay, so it floods. So what?

28
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.430
[NAMI]
Well, it worries me, that's all.

29
00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.960
I'll check into it later.

30
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.900
Come on, let's head back to the inn for
the time being.

31
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.280
[ELEVATOR GIRL A]
In compliance with

32
00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.380
the Aqua Laguna warning

33
00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.320
that was issued for the
entire island earlier today:

34
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.620
all docks on the
shipbuilding island are now

35
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.820
to be considered public
shelter and evacuation centers.

36
00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.290
Large crowds are expected,

37
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.330
so please take shelter
as quickly as possible.

38
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.400
Additionally, keep
in mind that Dock One

39
00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.370
is currently in
a dangerous state.

40
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.870
[CITIZEN A]
All right,
I'll put the iron board on.

41
00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.040
Hey Honey, you sure we
have everything we'll need?

42
00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.640
Yes... Now, come on.

43
00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.720
We need to take shelter in the shipyard.

44
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.230
[CITIZEN A]
Patience, patience!

45
00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.560
You gotta be careful sealing this board.

46
00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.360
If the inside of our
house gets flooded,

47
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.280
everything will be ruined.

48
00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.920
[CITIZEN B]
Hey! The wind
is starting to pick up!

49
00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.890
The waves will be
here anytime now!

50
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.920
Hurry! If we take too long,

51
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.590
those assassin pirates
are gonna show up, too!

52
00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:05.950
What?

53
00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.350
Where'd he disappear to?

54
00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.390
[CRAFTSMAN B]
I'm sure he went this way!

55
00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.090
[CRAFTSMAN C]
He's gotta be around here!

56
00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.030
[CRAFTSMAN A]
Okay.
You guys look over there!

57
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.380
[CRAFTSMAN B]
Right!

58
00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.780
[thinking]
What the hell is going on?

59
00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.950
Why're they chasing me?
I don't understand!

60
00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.230
Wait a sec! Is this why
everybody's after me?

61
00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.240
"Culprits in the
assassination plot"?

62
00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.370
Well that sucks.

63
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.040
Can't go back to the inn now...
I'll be out in the open.

64
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.910
Hey! Who goes
there? Who are you?

65
00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.180
Over here! There's a suspicious
guy hiding in the alley!

66
00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:55.320
<b>Innkeeper</b>

67
00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.140
You sure about this?
There's no mistake?

68
00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.430
I'm certain!

69
00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.870
They've been
staying here at the inn

70
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.370
since they
checked in last night!

71
00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.910
They took off just a little while ago.

72
00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.970
They're staying here?!

73
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.040
Yes, that's right!

74
00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.550
They still have lots of luggage left in
their room.

75
00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.130
I'm sure they'll be back for it sometime.

76
00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.610
Right! You guys
stay here, okay?

77
00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.250
The rest of you, search the
surrounding area with me.

78
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.450
Look sharp!
Leave no stone unturned.

79
00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.560
Does everybody got it?

80
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.570
[GROUP]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

81
00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.430
[CRAFTSMAN F]
Huh. No one's here.

82
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.450
Are you one hundred percent
certain that this is their ship?

83
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.880
There's no mistaking it!
Look up there!

84
00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.280
That's the flag of
the Straw Hat pirates!

85
00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.810
They probably already abandoned her.

86
00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.840
She's all worn out.

87
00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.080
[CRAFTSMAN I]
Did you find them?

88
00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.890
[CRAFTSMAN J]
No. They're gone.

89
00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.460
[CRAFTSMAN F]
There's
not much left on board.

90
00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.000
I'm pretty sure she was
abandoned and left to sink.

91
00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.930
Let's keep looking around.

92
00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.310
[thinking]
Who were those guys?

93
00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.880
Is there something going on in the city?

94
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.260
[CRAFTSMAN K]
Find anything?

95
00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.120
[CRAFTSMAN L]
Not a trace of them.

96
00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.900
[CRAFTSMAN K]
Dammit! Where are they?

97
00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.260
They sure are persistent.

98
00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.130
Hey, Luffy?

99
00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.830
Huh? What is it, Nami?

100
00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.710
Do you think everybody's okay?

101
00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.180
These guys are
all over the place!

102
00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:36.880
Chopper and Sanji
are probably safe

103
00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.250
because no one knows
their faces yet, but still.

104
00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.450
Come on, we need to hurry!

105
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.860
[NAMI]
Right!

106
00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.350
It looks like the sea
train's still in operation.

107
00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.260
I guess the noon departure has already
left.

108
00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.990
There's another one
scheduled for tonight,

109
00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.130
even in all this bad weather.

110
00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.270
The 11 PM, leaving for Enies Lobby.

111
00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.280
That sea train is
pretty impressive.

112
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.290
[CRAFTSMAN M]
Hey!
Any news on those pirates?

113
00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.450
[CRAFTSMAN N]
We've got nothing!

114
00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.520
[CRAFTSMAN O]
If we can
capture just one of those three

115
00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.990
from the wanted posters,

116
00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.890
we'll make 'em cough
up who the others are.

117
00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.230
[CRAFTSMAN M]
Hurry!
Before the waves get too high!

118
00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.310
[CHOPPER]
Maybe we can't find Robin

119
00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.880
because she got
on the sea train.

120
00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.820
Well, if she did that
would make things

121
00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.920
worse than they already are.

122
00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:24.790
Water Seven's too big an
area to cover on its own.

123
00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:25.990
What if...

124
00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.950
What if I did something to upset
her back at the bookstore?

125
00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.450
[SANJI]
Don't be ridiculous.
No way that's the reason.

126
00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.000
Hey! Excuse me!

127
00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:32.970
Have you seen a
beautiful woman

128
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.210
who kind of looks like this?

129
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.170
[CITIZEN D]
You mean the one who's

130
00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.100
about 20 years older
than that picture?

131
00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.440
If I had, I would've
told the newspapers

132
00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.420
or the Galley-La
Company about it.

133
00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.310
[CITIZEN D]
To think
she's an assassin.

134
00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.640
Kind of shocking, huh?

135
00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.230
I admire you for trying to
track down that criminal,

136
00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.670
but I suggest you find
yourself some shelter soon.

137
00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.640
Aqua Laguna is on its way!

138
00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.350
Take care!

139
00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.460
Things are getting dangerous around here.

140
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.700
What about the others?
Think they're okay?

141
00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.290
I'm sure Luffy's fine.

142
00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.490
Nami's the one that I'm
really worried about right now.

143
00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:15.100
[SANJI]
At any rate, this city's
becoming quite the ghost town.

144
00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.030
[CHOPPER]
The wind's really picking up.

145
00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.370
I'm sure most people are already in the
shelter.

146
00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.160
Where could she be?!

147
00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.150
Hey! Robin!

148
00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.650
Where are you?!

149
00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.930
[thinking]
That scent! Is it?

150
00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.000
Huh? Chopper! What is it?

151
00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.040
Chopper?

152
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.080
Hey! Wait for me!

153
00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.440
[thinking]
This way!

154
00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.010
Hey, Chopper!

155
00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.680
Chopper!

156
00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.320
Oo... Waaah!

157
00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:56.060
[tumbling sounds
followed by a thud]

158
00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.760
Are you all right?

159
00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.830
[SANJI]
Chopper! Did you hurt yourself?

160
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.930
There you are!

161
00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.800
You can't just go
running off like that!

162
00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.770
What in the hell is
the matter with you?

163
00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.870
One second, you're right beside me.

164
00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.370
[CHOPPER]
Robin!
[SANJI] It's Robin!

165
00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.750
Robin! Where in the
world have you been?

166
00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.650
Everyone's worried!

167
00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.890
We've been looking
for you everywhere!

168
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.960
Come on! Let's head
back to the inn!

169
00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.760
A lot's happened while you were gone.

170
00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.830
I'll explain everything on the way.

171
00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.260
This damn water's split us up.

172
00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.380
Hold on! I'll find
another way over there!

173
00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.760
Don't bother. It's all right.

174
00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.490
Stay where you are.

175
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.180
There's no need.

176
00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.560
Because I won't be coming back to you and
your crew.

177
00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:47.400
We're parting ways
here in this city.

178
00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:48.770
What the?

179
00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.340
What in the world
are you talking about?

180
00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.840
Oh wait, you mean
that stuff they said

181
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.260
about you in the newspaper?
Don't worry about it!

182
00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.360
None of us believes it.

183
00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:00.210
Pirates are falsely accused of crimes all
the time.

184
00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.280
We're easy targets.

185
00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.720
[ROBIN]
About that.

186
00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.310
I apologize for pinning such

187
00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.340
an unreasonable
crime on all of you.

188
00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.340
But as far as my involvement...

189
00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.080
Everything that was said in the newspaper
is true.

190
00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.300
Late last night, I broke
into the mayor's place

191
00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.060
of residence and shot him.

192
00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.830
No way.

193
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:24.270
Inside me, I carry a darkness that none of
you know about.

194
00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:28.880
One day, that darkness will be the end of
all of you.

195
00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:31.180
[AOKIJI]
Every organization
that she's had something

196
00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.240
to do with in the past
has been annihilated.

197
00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.490
Not one single, solitary
member escaped, except for her.

198
00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.890
[ROBIN]
I'm afraid you'll
be taking the fall

199
00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:42.670
for last night's attack
while I escape.

200
00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.220
And let me warn you.

201
00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.580
The situation will only get worse.

202
00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:49.380
What are you talking about?!
I don't understand!

203
00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:50.890
[ROBIN]
Why I'm doing it?

204
00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:53.720
There's no need for you to understand.

205
00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:56.930
Robin! What happened?

206
00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.070
You're not making any sense!

207
00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.940
This isn't like you at all!

208
00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:03.070
Please! We'll work
this out together!

209
00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.580
Although I only spent
a short time with you,

210
00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.640
from this day forward.

211
00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.940
We will never see each other again.

212
00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.570
Thank you for all of the kindness you've
shown me.

213
00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:18.270
Know that I'll never forget it.

214
00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.670
Goodbye.

215
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.510
[SANJI]
Wait...

216
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.250
No... please...

217
00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.510
This can't...

218
00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:45.150
This can't be happening.

219
00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.520
Hey!

220
00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.990
Come back!

221
00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:57.030
[SANJI]
Stop! You don't know
what you're saying! Robin!

222
00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.230
Wait! Please! Come back!

223
00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.130
Robin!

224
00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.480
I lost track of her scent.

225
00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.810
I see.

226
00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:24.780
Hey, Chopper.

227
00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.380
Hm?

228
00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:27.730
[SANJI]
Go meet up with
Luffy and the others

229
00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.340
and tell them everything that
happened between us and Robin.

230
00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:34.340
I don't want you to leave out a single
word.

231
00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.270
Sure.

232
00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.410
As for me, let's just
say I have a plan.

233
00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:42.410
I'll try to be careful.
We'll meet up later.

234
00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:44.950
[CRAFTSMAN B]
Where'd they go?

235
00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:47.400
[CRAFTSMAN C]
Check the alleys!

236
00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.500
[CRAFTSMAN D]
You don't think
they're on the rooftops, do you?

237
00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.790
[CRAFTSMAN F]
Damn it! We lost 'em!

238
00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.810
[CRAFTSMAN G]
I don't get it.
I'm sure they went this way.

239
00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.380
[CRAFTSMAN H]
We'd better keep moving.

240
00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.450
[CRAFTSMAN I]
All right,
but we should check

241
00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.480
inside the buildings, too.

242
00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.060
[CRAFTSMAN J]
Good.
We'll split up. Let's go!

243
00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.790
Yeah!

244
00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.520
[LUFFY]
Is it okay now?

245
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.360
Wait a sec.

246
00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.770
[CRAFTSMAN K]
Where'd you last see them?

247
00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.400
Just a little longer.

248
00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.790
[NAMI shrieks]

249
00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.420
Uhhh...

250
00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.600
I'm begging you.

251
00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.760
[SHOP OWNER A]
Are you crazy?

252
00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.240
I've gotta evacuate!
Stop pestering me!

253
00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:50.270
Come on.
I have money, okay?

254
00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.670
Here take it.

255
00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.920
I need as much lumber, tar, and rope as
this'll buy.

256
00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:55.850
Oh, and also some nails,

257
00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.560
latches and tin plates,
if you don't mind.

258
00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.560
[SHOP OWNER A]
I said I'm closing the shop.

259
00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.000
[USOPP]
It'll just
take a second, please.

260
00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:06.480
[USOPP's stomach growls]

261
00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:08.750
[sighs]

262
00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:09.920
Okay, kid.

263
00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.650
But I'm afraid this money
ain't gonna buy much for ya.

264
00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:15.840
Uh. Then... how
'bout I sell my tools?

265
00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.010
Will that make up for the rest?

266
00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:17.940
Hey, hey. Come on! Stop it!

267
00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:20.850
We don't do barter.

268
00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.750
This's the big city, you know.

269
00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.520
I'm sorry, but it's cash only.

270
00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.960
You win. But
let's make it quick.

271
00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.980
[SHOP OWNER A]
You sure
you're okay carrying that

272
00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:42.380
with all those injuries?

273
00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:45.580
Can't you get some friends
to help you out? Hey!

274
00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.550
[USOPP grunts]

275
00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.980
[SHOP OWNER A]
I knew this was a bad idea!

276
00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.080
Wait! This isn't gonna work!

277
00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:13.050
I'm fine. I got it.
This is nothing.

278
00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:13.750
[SHOP OWNER A]
Hey!

279
00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:15.480
Don't worry. I can do it.

280
00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.020
[SHOP OWNER A]
No, look.

281
00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.650
Here, take these.

282
00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:20.180
You're hungry, right?

283
00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:23.390
[stomach growls]

284
00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.140
[USOPP]
Th-Thank you.

285
00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.620
[SHOP OWNER A]
Sure thing.
Try to be careful.

286
00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.250
Good luck out there, kid!

287
00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.350
[USOPP]
Mm-mm.

288
00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.220
These are good.

289
00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.120
Really good.

290
00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:56.550
Guess that guy was pretty nice after all.

291
00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.910
The waves sure are getting high,
aren't they?

292
00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:21.100
Don't worry, Merry.
You're gonna be just fine!

293
00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:34.250
After all, you flew in the sky,
remember?

294
00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.620
You've got nothing
to be afraid of!

295
00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:43.020
[loud crashing]

296
00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:51.110
Oh ho ho! Whoa, what's
got you riled up, big guy?

297
00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.910
C'mon Franky,
you can tell us!

298
00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.190
What's up, bro?

299
00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.330
AARRGH!

300
00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.830
I got so much rage inside me,

301
00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:15.900
I feel another rampage
comin' on right about now!

302
00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.270
[MOZU]
Hey, wait for me, bro,
don't rampage alone!

303
00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:22.020
As always, thanks for the drinks,
Blueno!

304
00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.980
Hahaha!

305
00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.160
What got into him all of a sudden?

306
00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.860
Is there something going on?

307
00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.070
Beats me.

308
00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:36.970
Never can tell with that guy.

309
00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:40.100
Only idiots know what idiots are thinking.

310
00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.310
Looks like the crowd cleared out.

311
00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:56.100
Yeah, no thanks to you!

312
00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.430
I'll have you know that Luffy
and I had a perfectly good

313
00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:01.700
hiding place until you lead
that angry mob straight to us!

314
00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.530
Like I said, with that
many people looking,

315
00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:05.610
they were gonna
find you anyway.

316
00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.240
Oh yeah, that reminds me.

317
00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.380
How did you know we
were down there, Chopper?

318
00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:10.560
Your smell.

319
00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.280
Ah... I shoulda known.

320
00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:15.200
But wait, wasn't Sanji with you?

321
00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.150
Well, he was.

322
00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.470
No way! That doesn't
make any sense!

323
00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.680
Did Robin really
say that to you?!

324
00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.790
[ZORO]
We were prepared
for this, weren't we?

325
00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:52.560
After all, Robin was our enemy before we
let her join the crew.

326
00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.330
This might be our only
chance to find out the truth.

327
00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.530
So we shouldn't run away.

328
00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:03.340
There's still lot of things
we don't know about Robin.

329
00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.780
Now it's time to decide if she's a friend
or a foe.

330
00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:10.990
[ROBIN]
The

331
00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.480
situation will get worse.

332
00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:17.080
From this day forward we will
never see each other again.

333
00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:23.160
[ZORO]
You're sure?

334
00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.820
That's all she said, Chopper?

335
00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:27.790
Mmm.

336
00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:30.030
If she says she won't
see us after today

337
00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.570
and things are gonna get worse,

338
00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.180
maybe that means
the attack on Iceburg

339
00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.940
was just a warm-up
and she has something

340
00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.380
even bigger
planned for tonight.

341
00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:43.590
I don't know why
Robin's doing any of this,

342
00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.720
so it's hard to make a guess
as to what she's planning.

343
00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.690
But seeing how much
commotion her first attack

344
00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:49.920
on the mayor caused,

345
00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.170
there's only one way
to make things worse.

346
00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:55.900
In other words,
she'll murder him.

347
00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:01.340
[ZORO]
I think that's what she's
trying to tell us, at least.

348
00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.150
Also since she told Chopper

349
00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.880
that she'll be pinning
the crime on us,

350
00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.020
it could be that she's feeding
us all these little hints

351
00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:11.310
to try and lure us out
to the crime scene tonight.

352
00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:12.270
Think so?

353
00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:14.320
If that is her plan,
it would be convenient

354
00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:16.260
for her if we did
happen to show up.

355
00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:18.750
Since that would put us
at the scene of the crime.

356
00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.160
You say you don't
know what she's thinking,

357
00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.020
but it sound to me like you've

358
00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:23.760
already decided that she's our enemy!

359
00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.030
I'm talking about possibilities here,
that's all.

360
00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:26.950
We should always be prepared

361
00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:29.820
for the worst-case
scenario, understand?

362
00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.820
If I get locked into a
single line of thinking,

363
00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:34.920
it'll only slow me down.
If she's my friend,

364
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.690
I have to be ready to forgive

365
00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:40.630
but if she's my enemy
I have to be ready to fight.

366
00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:48.600
Our best chance to settle
this is tonight. Are we going?

367
00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.140
Of course.

368
00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:53.730
It's not that
I object to the plan

369
00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.240
but we're still
forgetting something.

370
00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.000
Sanji said he saw Robin walking

371
00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.640
with someone in
a mask, remember?

372
00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.280
Obviously that wasn't one of us,

373
00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:04.640
but Iceburg said
exactly the same thing.

374
00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:05.780
That he was attacked by Robin

375
00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.950
and a large man in a mask
that he didn't recognize.

376
00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:11.240
Whoever he is,
I bet he's the reason

377
00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.210
Robin is doing
all of this stuff.

378
00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.710
Yeah! That means
it isn't her fault

379
00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.400
and we just need to beat
the real bad guy. Right?

380
00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:19.640
That's the ideal situation.

381
00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.890
But on the other hand,

382
00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.710
it's also possible that this
guy is one of Robin's friends.

383
00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.370
The problem is we
don't have much to go

384
00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.810
on other than
"a big man in a mask."

385
00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.210
So where do we even start?

386
00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:31.350
I mean, what is our goal here?

387
00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:34.120
We find Robin and capture her.

388
00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:38.640
[LUFFY]
That's the only way
we'll ever know the truth.

389
00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:39.640
[ZORO]
You're right.

390
00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:41.880
We're wasting time here trying to figure
it out.

391
00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.210
Just one thing.

392
00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:45.720
Robin won't be easy to catch.

393
00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:47.420
After all, the World
Government's been trying

394
00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:51.140
for 20 years and it
still hasn't happened.

395
00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:54.410
Like he said, it's the only way we'll
really know for sure.

396
00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:58.360
Yeah. Let's settle
this right now!

397
00:21:58.360 --> 00:21:59.900
[LUFFY]
Right.

398
00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.720
Come on. Galley-La's waiting.

399
00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:12.260
Damn. It's late.
Where'd Straw Hat run off to?

400
00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:14.330
[CRAFTSMAN C]
Paulie! We gotta go!

401
00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:17.050
All these streets are gonna flood before
long!

402
00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.690
All right. Let's head back.

403
00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.820
I'm going to the main office.

404
00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:22.830
Sounds good, boss.

405
00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:25.350
You heard him, guys,
time to move out!

406
00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:30.960
[FRANKY]
Get out here and
fight me, Straw Hat!

407
00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:35.070
Where are you?! Stop hiding!

408
00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.080
I thought that little
turd had some backbone,

409
00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:41.240
but I guess I was wrong.

410
00:22:41.270 --> 00:22:43.140
Won't even show his face.

411
00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:44.810
I know what you're saying, bro,

412
00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:47.080
but to be fair, the whole
island is hunting him down

413
00:22:47.110 --> 00:22:48.110
right now, you know?

414
00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:50.080
Exactly! I bet he's hiding,

415
00:22:50.110 --> 00:22:52.880
if he hasn't been
caught already.

416
00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:54.550
By the way, what's
with this weird crab

417
00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:55.550
walk thing all of a sudden.

418
00:22:55.550 --> 00:22:57.450
If we face the front,
then the wind catches

419
00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:01.550
our hair and we blow away!

420
00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:03.520
Speaking of which, the
weather isn't the only thing

421
00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:05.190
that's out of control today.

422
00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:06.390
[MOZU]
Tell me about it.

423
00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:08.990
It's like you've got a rampage going on
inside you, too.

424
00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:13.030
Shut up. I'm just like
that this week, okay?

425
00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:14.750
[ZAMBAI]
Hey bro!

426
00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:16.760
[GROUP]
– Hey, it's bro! Hey, bro!
– Hey, it's bro! Hey, bro!

427
00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:19.370
[MOZU]
Well, if it isn't Zambai!

428
00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:22.420
Tell me, tell me that you
beat up those stupid Straw Hats.

429
00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:23.920
No, but I tried to.

430
00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.090
Some angry mob showed up,

431
00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:27.020
got in the way,
then Luffy took off.

432
00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:28.430
[GROUP]
– Huh?
– Huh?

433
00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:30.360
Are those guys lucky or what?

434
00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:33.360
When you're on a rampage, nobody survives!

435
00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:35.430
That's weird. I wondered
why that weak dude

436
00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:37.920
with the long nose was
fixing the ship on his own.

437
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.920
I figured that you'd wrecked
up the rest of the crew

438
00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:42.940
so bad that he was the only one
left who could do anything.

439
00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:45.490
Wait. You found one of 'em?!

440
00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:47.450
Yeah, on their ship.

441
00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:52.020
[FRANKY chuckles]

442
00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:55.190
Well, that's just fine,
'cause all we need is one.

443
00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:56.390
In other words,

444
00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:59.830
we'll use that loser as bait
to lure out the rest of 'em.

445
00:23:59.860 --> 00:24:04.070
Whoa, Bro's got his
bad guy face on, guys.

446
00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:05.800
All right, you
good-for-nothings,

447
00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:07.040
I want you to march
through the town

448
00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:09.170
and spread the word for me.

449
00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:11.220
Say "we've got Long-Nose

450
00:24:11.250 --> 00:24:13.150
and if you don't want him
swimming with the fishes,

451
00:24:13.240 --> 00:24:16.010
then come to the
warehouse under the bridge."

452
00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:19.380
Tell 'em Franky sent ya.

453
00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:22.080
[chuckles]

454
00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:24.350
In the meantime,
I'll go nab Long Nose

455
00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:26.920
so we can make good
on our little threat.

456
00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:30.390
You got it, Bro! I swear
we won't let you down!

457
00:24:43.030 --> 00:24:45.400
It's my special bed.

458
00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:48.510
<b>Shipyard Basement Storeroom
(Evacuation Center)</b>

459
00:24:45.430 --> 00:24:49.070
[CHILDREN]
– Aqua Laguna! Aqua Laguna!
– Aqua Laguna! Aqua Laguna!

460
00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:53.100
Aqua Laguna is coming for you!

461
00:24:53.140 --> 00:24:54.810
[CHILD A]
Here comes a big wave!

462
00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:56.770
[laughter, play shrieks]

463
00:24:56.810 --> 00:24:58.180
So do you know
what's going on

464
00:24:58.210 --> 00:24:59.410
with those Straw Hats?

465
00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:00.280
I'm not sure.

466
00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:02.050
I don't think they've caught them yet.

467
00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:04.050
Tsk! Still on the loose!

468
00:25:04.080 --> 00:25:05.750
Ah... That's no good!

469
00:25:05.780 --> 00:25:08.390
And with everyone so
worked up about the storm,

470
00:25:08.420 --> 00:25:10.350
they'll have the perfect
chance to attack again.

471
00:25:10.410 --> 00:25:11.680
And what I heard,
is that tonight,

472
00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:17.070
all the craftsmen from
the Galley-La Company

473
00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:19.670
will be guarding the main
office to protect the mayor.

474
00:25:19.700 --> 00:25:23.340
Whoa, that's a really
big deal, isn't it?

475
00:25:23.370 --> 00:25:25.910
[CITIZEN F]
How many people
have the Straw Hats got, anyway?

476
00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:29.340
[CITIZEN G]
Some say 50.
Some say 100 or even more!

477
00:25:29.380 --> 00:25:32.820
Remember, the captain's got a
100 million bounty on his head.

478
00:25:32.850 --> 00:25:36.120
For all we know, he could be
sending an army of 3,000 men

479
00:25:36.150 --> 00:25:38.190
to fight the
shipwrights as we speak!

480
00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:41.020
Are you kidding?!
That sounds really bad!

481
00:25:46.970 --> 00:25:47.900
[CRAFTSMAN M]
All right, men,

482
00:25:47.940 --> 00:25:50.840
hold your formation
and don't give an inch!

483
00:25:50.870 --> 00:25:52.300
[GROUP]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

484
00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:55.110
Don't even let a single
fly get through, got it?!

485
00:25:55.140 --> 00:25:57.710
[GROUP]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

486
00:26:06.710 --> 00:26:12.590
<b>Outside Iceburg's Bedroom</b>

487
00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:15.140
Bring it on! Wahahaha!

488
00:26:16.300 --> 00:26:18.740
What's wrong with you?!

489
00:26:18.830 --> 00:26:21.140
Would you please
be quiet, Tiletone?!

490
00:26:22.060 --> 00:26:22.820
[LULU]
I heard the Straw Hats

491
00:26:22.860 --> 00:26:25.130
weren't spotted on
the sea train.

492
00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:28.980
That means they're still here on the
island somewhere.

493
00:26:28.980 --> 00:26:31.000
Still. They'd be complete
idiots if they tried

494
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.140
to show up with all
of these guards around.

495
00:26:33.170 --> 00:26:34.140
Yeah, you'd think,

496
00:26:34.220 --> 00:26:35.420
but that didn't
stop the dumbass

497
00:26:35.450 --> 00:26:39.270
that barged in
here earlier, did it?

498
00:26:39.270 --> 00:26:42.070
We gotta be ready for anything.

499
00:26:42.070 --> 00:26:46.610
[ICEBURG]
Mwell, this is
reassuring, but it's a bit much.

500
00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:48.920
<b>Bedroom</b>

501
00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:49.280
They wanted to do this for you.

502
00:26:49.310 --> 00:26:50.920
I'm not royalty.

503
00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:52.660
Pardon me sir,
but why on earth

504
00:26:52.750 --> 00:26:56.690
did you put Nico Robin's
wanted poster up on your wall?

505
00:26:56.720 --> 00:26:58.590
It bother you?

506
00:27:00.390 --> 00:27:00.890
A bit.

507
00:27:01.790 --> 00:27:03.630
Hmm...

508
00:27:05.440 --> 00:27:07.190
It's better if you don't know.

509
00:27:10.950 --> 00:27:13.860
That girl is a demon.

510
00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:43.720
[CHOPPER]
There sure are
a lot of people out there.

511
00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:44.890
It's a little far, too.

512
00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:47.280
It'll be fine if you rocket through the
window, right?

513
00:27:47.290 --> 00:27:49.190
After Robin shows up, I mean.

514
00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:51.250
That' right. If we
make a commotion first,

515
00:27:51.280 --> 00:27:53.820
then they'll just sneak in while
we're dealing with the guards.

516
00:27:53.850 --> 00:27:55.720
Let's be patient.

517
00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:56.660
[CRAFTSMAN M]
Get ready!

518
00:27:56.690 --> 00:27:59.660
Strike at anything
that moves, men! Got it?

519
00:27:59.690 --> 00:28:02.360
[GROUP]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!
